          "start_ms": null,
          "status": "needs-review",
          "text": "Description: On December 30, 2014, at 4:20 a.m., a witness observed the north-south passage of a matte yellow sphere. The passage was quickly obscured by trees. No noise or trail was noticed. Only one testimony was collected. Given the information presented in the investigation report, and pending further information from the witness in response to our request, the lack of data does not allow for a conclusion in favor of any hypothesis. This testimony is of average consistency: fairly precise and detailed but old. Only one eyewitness and no photo or video documentation. The observation could be somewhat strange, however, the age of the testimony prevents truly evaluating its strangeness. This case is provisionally classified as \"C\" as an observation of an unidentified phenomenon at this stage, the significant lack of elements not allowing for a solid opinion.",
